Subject: [PATCH] init: avoid static destructors during container shutdown

SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

The non-reboot-capable path runs after service shutdown, synchronization
and unmount. Calling exit() there invokes static C++ destructors, including
a joinable thread's destructor, and aborts the container's init process.
Use _exit() for this terminal path. Leave reboot-capable systems unchanged.

--- a/init/reboot_utils.cpp
+++ b/init/reboot_utils.cpp
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@
     if (!IsRebootCapable()) {
         // On systems where init does not have the capability of rebooting the
         // device, just exit cleanly.
-        exit(0);
+        _exit(0);
     }
 
     switch (cmd) {
